<p>The average driver spends over an hour daily inside their vehicle. During that time, they touch the steering wheel, adjust vents, eat snacks, and transport passengers who bring dust, pollen, and bacteria along for the ride. A surface-level vacuum captures loose debris but leaves behind oils, allergens, and microbes embedded in fabrics and plastics. Interior steam cleaning reaches deeper—using heat and minimal moisture to sanitise without the risks associated with soaking upholstery.</p>
