<h2>Why Headlights Turn Yellow in India</h2>
<p>Modern headlamp lenses use polycarbonate plastic rather than glass—lighter and impact-resistant but vulnerable to UV degradation. Punjab's intense sun, combined with pollution and road chemicals, oxidises the outer lens layer within three to five years. Yellowed, hazy headlights reduce light output by up to 80 percent, creating genuine safety hazards during monsoon night driving when visibility is already compromised.</p>

<h2>Restoration vs Replacement</h2>
<p>Replacement headlamp assemblies for premium vehicles cost ₹15,000–80,000 per pair. Professional restoration achieves 90–95 percent clarity recovery for a fraction of that price—when performed correctly with proper UV sealant application afterward. Restoration without sealant fails within months as fresh plastic surface re-oxidises immediately.</p>

<h2>The Professional Restoration Process</h2>
<h3>Multi-Stage Wet Sanding</h3>
<p>Technicians progress through increasingly fine abrasives—typically 600, 1000, 2000, and 3000 grit—removing the oxidised layer evenly without distorting lens shape. Masking protects surrounding paint throughout.</p>
<h3>Machine Polishing</h3>
<p>After sanding, polishing compounds restore optical clarity and remove fine scratches. This stage determines how crystal-clear the final result appears.</p>
<h3>UV-Resistant Sealant or PPF</h3>
<p>Critical final step: apply dedicated headlamp clear coat or precision-cut PPF. This barrier blocks UV penetration and maintains clarity for two to four years depending on product and parking conditions.</p>

<h2>Maintenance After Restoration</h2>
<p>Wash headlights gently—avoid aggressive scrubbing on unprotected lenses. Apply headlamp sealant annually if not covered by PPF. Park facing away from direct sun when possible. During full vehicle ceramic coating service, ensure headlights receive compatible protection products.</p>

<h2>When Replacement Is Necessary</h2>
<p>Deep internal moisture, cracked housings, or lenses sanded previously multiple times may warrant replacement. Our technicians assess honestly during detailing appointments rather than attempting restoration on unsuitable units.</p>

