<h2>Wheels Tell the Story of Vehicle Care</h2>
<p>Experienced buyers and enthusiasts look at wheels first. Brake dust baked onto alloy surfaces, corroded lug nuts, and cracked tyre sidewalls signal neglect regardless of how shiny the body panels appear. Proper wheel and tyre detailing requires dedicated tools, chemistry, and patience that general washing skips entirely.</p>

<h2>Understanding Brake Dust</h2>
<p>Brake pads shed metallic particles that embed in wheel clear coat and porous alloy finishes. In Punjab's stop-start traffic, dust accumulates rapidly—sometimes visibly within days of washing. Iron particles oxidise into orange rust spots that conventional shampoo cannot dissolve. Iron removers (fallout removers) chemically transform these particles so they rinse away without scrubbing.</p>

<h2>The Complete Wheel Detailing Process</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Cool wheels first:</strong> Never clean hot wheels—products dry instantly and stain</li>
<li><strong>Apply iron remover:</strong> Allow dwell time until colour change indicates reaction</li>
<li><strong>Agitate with soft brushes:</strong> Different sizes for face, barrel, and lug recesses</li>
<li><strong>Clean tyre sidewalls:</strong> Dedicated tyre brush and APC removes browning</li>
<li><strong>Rinse thoroughly:</strong> Residual chemicals stain paint if dripped on bodywork</li>
<li><strong>Dry completely:</strong> Prevent water spots on machined faces</li>
<li><strong>Apply tyre dressing:</strong> Water-based, matte finish for modern appearance</li>
</ul>

<h2>Protecting Alloy Wheels</h2>
<p>Ceramic coating service applied to wheels creates hydrophobic surfaces that resist brake dust bonding. Coated wheels clean in half the time during maintenance washes and maintain their finish years longer than unprotected alloys. Given Punjab's humidity, coated wheels also resist corrosion on bare aluminium exposed by curb damage.</p>

<h2>Tyre Care Beyond Appearance</h2>
<p>Tyre dressing is cosmetic, but sidewall cleaning reveals damage—bulges, cuts, and perishing rubber—that affects safety. Check pressures monthly; Punjab's heat increases pressure beyond recommended levels if set when cool. Rotate tyres per manufacturer schedule to ensure even wear.</p>

<h2>Common Mistakes</h2>
<p>Using the same wash mitt on wheels and paint transfers abrasive brake dust to body panels. Acidic wheel cleaners etch clear-coated alloys permanently. Over-shiny tyre dressings sling onto bodywork during driving. Professional detailers at Diamond Steam Car Wash use wheel-specific tools and products isolated from paint workflows entirely.</p>

<h2>Maintenance Frequency</h2>
<p>Deep wheel detail monthly for daily city drivers. Biweekly quick clean with iron remover on heavily used vehicles. Combine with your regular professional steam wash for consistent results. Showroom wheels are achievable—they simply demand the attention most quick washes deliberately omit.</p>

