        'content' => <<<'HTML'
<h2>Matte Paint Is Not Just a Different Colour</h2>
<p>Factory matte and satin finishes—popular on SUVs, sports cars, and limited editions—use clear coats with diffusing additives that scatter light rather than reflecting it uniformly. This chemistry creates the distinctive flat appearance but also makes the surface more porous, more stain-prone, and impossible to correct with traditional polishing without creating permanent glossy patches.</p>

<h2>Unique Challenges in Indian Climate</h2>
<p>Punjab's pollution, tree sap, bird droppings, and monsoon mineral deposits stain matte paint more readily than gloss. Fingerprints and improper washing leave visible marks that do not buff out. UV exposure can cause uneven fading that is particularly noticeable on matte surfaces where gloss variation reads as damage.</p>

<h2>Washing Matte and Satin Paint</h2>
<h3>Products and Technique</h3>
<p>Use pH-neutral shampoo specifically labelled safe for matte finishes. Never use wax, glaze, polish, or standard ceramic coatings designed for gloss paint—these alter the surface texture permanently. Wash in straight-line motions with soft mitts; circular scrubbing creates visible patterns on matte clear coat.</p>
<h3>Steam Wash Compatibility</h3>
<p>Professional steam wash is safe for matte paint when performed by technicians trained on special finishes. Heat and minimal contact remove contamination without products that add shine. Always inform your detailer about matte finish before service begins.</p>

<h2>Protection Options for Matte Vehicles</h2>
<p>Dedicated matte paint sealants and matte-specific PPF preserve appearance without adding gloss. Standard ceramic coating service products are incompatible—matte-specific formulations exist from premium brands and require specialist application. PPF provides excellent protection for matte finishes since it can be replaced without touching factory paint texture.</p>

<h2>What to Never Do</h2>
<ul>
<li>Machine polish or compound matte panels</li>
<li>Use quick detailer sprays with gloss enhancers</li>
