        'excerpt' => 'Fabric and leather interiors need different cleaning approaches. Professional methods, products, and maintenance schedules for Indian car cabins. Expert guidance from Diamond Steam Car Wash, Punjab.',
        'content' => <<<'HTML'
<h2>One Cabin, Multiple Materials</h2>
<p>Modern vehicle interiors combine fabric, leather, synthetic leather, alcantara, vinyl, and carpet—sometimes within a single seat. Using leather conditioner on fabric stains it permanently. Shampooing leather causes shrinkage and cracking. Understanding material-specific cleaning methods prevents expensive upholstery damage while achieving genuine cleanliness rather than surface-level fragrance masking.</p>

<h2>Fabric Upholstery Cleaning</h2>
<h3>Challenges in Punjab</h3>
<p>Humidity prevents fabric from drying completely after wet shampooing, encouraging mould in foam cushions beneath. Food spills, monsoon wet clothing, and dust create odour sources that persist until deep extraction removes contamination from fibre depth.</p>
<h3>Professional Fabric Methods</h3>
<p>Steam extraction loosens grime with heat then extracts with vacuum equipment—using less water than traditional shampoo while achieving superior sanitisation. Enzyme treatments break down organic stains from food and beverages. Fabric protectant applied after cleaning repels future spills.</p>
<h3>Home Maintenance</h3>
<p>Weekly vacuuming with crevice tool. Immediate blotting of spills—never rub. Baking soda overnight on odours before vacuuming. Professional deep clean every three to four months.</p>

<h2>Leather Upholstery Cleaning</h2>
<h3>Challenges in Punjab</h3>
<p>Heat and UV through windows dry leather rapidly. Sweat and oils from bare skin accelerate wear on bolsters. Denim dye transfers onto light leather permanently without prompt cleaning.</p>
<h3>Professional Leather Methods</h3>
<p>pH-balanced leather cleaner applied with soft brushes, followed by steam on low setting for perforation cleaning, then immediate conditioning with compatible products. Never leave leather damp in humid conditions.</p>
<h3>Home Maintenance</h3>
<p>Monthly wipe with damp microfibre. Quarterly conditioning with approved products. Sunshades to reduce UV exposure. Avoid jeans contact on light leather when possible.</p>

<h2>Alcantara and Suede-Like Materials</h2>
<p>These premium materials require specialist cleaning—water and generic products destroy the nap texture. Professional detailers use dedicated alcantara brushes and cleaners. Never attempt home shampooing on alcantara.</p>

<h2>Comparison Summary</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Moisture tolerance:</strong> Fabric handles more water with proper extraction; leather needs minimal moisture</li>
<li><strong>Cleaning frequency:</strong> Fabric needs more frequent deep cleaning; leather needs more frequent conditioning</li>
<li><strong>Stain risk:</strong> Fabric absorbs; leather surface-stains but cracks if neglected</li>
<li><strong>Professional method:</strong> Steam extraction for fabric; steam plus conditioner for leather</li>
</ul>

<h2>Integrated Interior Service</h2>
<p>Diamond Steam Car Wash assesses every interior material during service and applies appropriate techniques panel by panel. Mixed-material cabins—common in premium SUVs—receive customised treatment rather than one-product-fits-all shortcuts. Book an interior steam cleaning and let specialists handle the complexity your cabin deserves.</p>
